Credits

No third-party code is included. The drivers use only Ubiquiti's official
UniFi Protect Integration API, as documented at https://developer.ui.com
(the OpenAPI specifications of UniFi Protect 5.3.48, 6.0.53, 6.1.79 and
6.2.83). How the Control4 camera proxy behaves in the field was learned from
the open-source C4-UnifiProtect drivers (https://github.com/efic1/C4-UnifiProtect,
MIT License); no code was copied from them.

Control4 interfaces follow the public Snap One DriverWorks documentation
(https://snap-one.github.io/docs-driverworks-fundamentals/). The WebSocket
client is a new implementation of RFC 6455.

The test fixtures in tests/ follow the official API schema and describe a
made-up home; names, addresses and ids in them are invented.
